# Access-tier annotations for the EU PPWR extension (ESPR Article 9 tiers).
# One entry per term; merged into the module by scripts/build-json.ts.
#
# Re-curated with per-term oec:accessLevelRationale and oec:accessLevelSource,
# grounded in the Packaging and Packaging Waste Regulation (EU) 2025/40. The
# PPWR is in force, but its recyclability-grade delegated acts (Art. 6) and
# harmonised-labelling implementing acts (Art. 12) are still pending and the
# labelling obligations apply only from 2028, so no term is locked via
# oec:accessLevelMandatedBy: deployments may tighten (never loosen) these
# defaults at runtime. Terms not listed default to AuthorizedOnly.

@prefix euppwr: <https://ref.openepcis.io/extensions/eu/ppwr/> .
@prefix oec:    <https://ref.openepcis.io/extensions/common/core/> .


# --- Public: on-pack labelling, packaging classification and the
# --- recyclability grade/methodology consumers and sorters rely on ---

euppwr:hasPackagingTier oec:defaultAccessLevel oec:Public ;
    oec:accessLevelRationale "The sales/grouped/transport classification (PPWR Art. 3) is basic packaging typing visible from the packaging itself and needed to interpret every other packaging claim." ;
    oec:accessLevelSource <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2025/40> .
euppwr:harmonisedSymbol oec:defaultAccessLevel oec:Public ;
    oec:accessLevelRationale "PPWR Art. 12 harmonised labels are printed on the packaging for consumers and separate-collection schemes, so their digital reference is inherently public (label formats pending implementing acts, hence not locked)." ;
    oec:accessLevelSource <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2025/40> .
euppwr:hasRecyclabilityGrade oec:defaultAccessLevel oec:Public ;
    oec:accessLevelRationale "The PPWR Art. 6 recyclability performance grade is a consumer- and scheme-facing band (grading criteria pending delegated acts, hence not locked)." ;
    oec:accessLevelSource <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2025/40> .
euppwr:designForRecyclingMethodology oec:defaultAccessLevel oec:Public ;
    oec:accessLevelRationale "Naming the design-for-recycling methodology (e.g. RecyClass) is the transparency that makes the public recyclability grade verifiable." ;
    oec:accessLevelSource <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2025/40> .

# --- Public: Article 12(2) reuse QR data — exactly the information the
# --- reuse data carrier must make available to end users ---

euppwr:hasReuseInformation oec:defaultAccessLevel oec:Public ;
    oec:accessLevelRationale "PPWR Art. 12(2): availability of the re-use system, collection points and trips/rotations (or the average estimation) are exactly the information the reuse QR code must make available to users (label formats pending implementing acts, hence not locked)." ;
    oec:accessLevelSource <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2025/40> .
euppwr:hasReuseSystemScope oec:defaultAccessLevel oec:Public ;
    oec:accessLevelRationale "The local/national/Union-wide availability of the re-use system is Art. 12(2) end-user information served through the reuse data carrier." ;
    oec:accessLevelSource <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2025/40> .
euppwr:reuseSystemName oec:defaultAccessLevel oec:Public ;
    oec:accessLevelRationale "Naming the re-use system (Annex VI system operator) is Art. 12(2) end-user information that makes the reuse claim actionable." ;
    oec:accessLevelSource <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2025/40> .
euppwr:collectionPointsUrl oec:defaultAccessLevel oec:Public ;
    oec:accessLevelRationale "Information on collection points is explicitly part of the Art. 12(2) reuse information made available through the QR code." ;
    oec:accessLevelSource <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2025/40> .
euppwr:rotationCount oec:defaultAccessLevel oec:Public ;
    oec:accessLevelRationale "Art. 12(2): the reuse data carrier facilitates the tracking of the packaging and the calculation of trips and rotations; the calculated count is user-facing reuse information." ;
    oec:accessLevelSource <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2025/40> .
euppwr:averageRotationsEstimate oec:defaultAccessLevel oec:Public ;
    oec:accessLevelRationale "The average estimation is the Art. 12(2) fallback where per-item trip/rotation calculation is not feasible, and is user-facing reuse information like the calculated count." ;
    oec:accessLevelSource <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2025/40> .

# --- AuthorizedOnly: deposit-return / take-back operational event data ---

euppwr:containerCondition oec:defaultAccessLevel oec:AuthorizedOnly ;
    oec:accessLevelRationale "The observed condition of a returned item is operational routing data of the deposit-return system (PPWR Arts. 27, 50), not consumer product information." ;
    oec:accessLevelSource <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2025/40> .
euppwr:depositRefundIssued oec:defaultAccessLevel oec:AuthorizedOnly ;
    oec:accessLevelRationale "Per-return refund amounts are operational financial event data of the deposit-return scheme (PPWR Art. 50); the static deposit amount is served publicly via GS1 master data instead." ;
    oec:accessLevelSource <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2025/40> .
